   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening leadership</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific is currently in a globally contested foreign policy space.  In 2023, an Australia Awards alumni Dr &apos;Ungatea Kata with her expertise and leadership skills alongside financial support from the Australian High Commission&apos;s office conducted a national Poll to capture Tongans opinions about the world, during this interesting period of time.  This is the first time such a national poll has been conducted in Tonga, to gauge Tongan people&apos;s attitudes towards global powers, confidence in world leaders, safety and threats to Tonga&apos;s interest, security and defence policy, relationship with superpowers, democracy at home and abroad, economic trade, climate change and Tongan foreign policy and foreign aid.  With the significant role played by Dr Kata, DFAT has a broader understanding on areas need strengthening.</narrative>
    </description>
